From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] android: skip redundant NV12 GPU finish after readback

The Android GPU software-ISP path reads the rendered RGBA intermediate with
glReadPixels() before converting it into the CPU-mapped NV12 output buffer.
glReadPixels() is synchronous and cannot return until the preceding draw is
complete, so the unconditional glFinish() afterwards repeats a full GPU
wait on every NV12 frame. Keep the finish for direct RGB DMA-BUF output,
where the emitted buffer still contains GPU writes.

This is an Android-only performance candidate. It does not change stream
formats, shaders, buffer ownership or the CPU conversion path.

Signed-off-by: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
index fed24f8..22b09e2 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -872,7 +872,13 @@ void DebayerEGL::process(uint32_t frame, FrameBuffer *input, FrameBuffer *output
 	}
 	inDmaSyncer.reset();
 
-	egl_.syncOutput();
+	/*
+	 * convertRgbaToNv12() has already completed a synchronous glReadPixels()
+	 * and written the output from the CPU. A second full GPU wait is
+	 * redundant for NV12, but remains required for direct RGB DMA-BUF output.
+	 */
+	if (!outputIsNv12_)
+		egl_.syncOutput();
 	bench_.finishFrame();
 
 	outputBufferReady.emit(output);
-- 
